\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  c.bank says ready to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  on market if needed\b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 2018\par 21:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Elena Fabrichnaya\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Oct 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on markets if necessary to support the prices of certain assets in the event of a crisis, the bank's First Deputy Governor Ksenia Yudayeva said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Russian assets have been under pressure since 2014 when the first round of western sanctions were imposed on Moscow for annexing Crimea from Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The rouble and Russian stocks and government bonds remain very sensitive to news of or speculation over any further restrictions.\par \par \uc2 A market selloff over fears of possible new U.S. sanctions drove the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to increase interest rates last month for the first time since 2014.\par \par \uc2 "In general, in case of an urgent need, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has an option of buying certain assets on the market depending which market has a risk emerging," Yudayeva told parliament on Tuesday. She did not specify say which assets the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might buy.\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Kolychev\uc2 , a deputy finance minister, said separately on Tuesday he believed the rouble might need the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's assistance most in the case of new western sanctions.\par \par \uc2 "So most likely, the market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are more related to the (Russian) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than... other assets," he said.\par \par \uc2 Yudayeva also said on Tuesday that most Russian banks would be sustainable under risk scenarios and should market volatility increase. (Reporting by Elena Fabrichnaya, Writing by Andrey Kuzmin and Katya Golubkova; Editing by Jon Boyle and John Stonestreet) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-10-16T20:00:59.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020181016eeag03ao9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
