\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Russian assets bounce as U.S. delays new sanctions\b0\par\par\uc2 894 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 2018\par 11:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LONDON, April 17 (Reuters) - Russian stocks and bonds rallied on Tuesday as the U.S. held off imposing fresh sanctions, though geopolitical tensions remained high and forecast-beating Chinese data did little to cheer markets with emerging stocks trading at one-week lows.\par \par \uc2 Russian stocks bounced 1.7 percent, Russian sovereign dollar bonds rose across the curve, and five-year credit default swaps fell after the U.S. delayed imposing additional sanctions on Russia.\par \par \uc2 Russian assets suffered last week after the U.S. administration slapped sanctions on a number of Russian businessmen and their companies.\par \par \uc2 "Some of the price action looked like an over-reaction, for example in the Russian bonds, so you get people buying it back," said Koon Chow, a strategist at UBP, who expects Russian assets to keep strengthening from here.\par \par \uc2 "If anything, the geopolitical developments will strengthen Russian policymakers' resolve to run a very conservative economic policy, which means your economy is less vulnerable to geopolitical-related developments."\par \par \uc2 The rouble remained volatile, weakening 0.8 percent after firming in early trade. U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has accused both Russia and China of devaluing their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  while the U.S. raises interest rates. \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets following the rouble's sharp fall last week.\par \par \uc2 Broader emerging markets also remained under pressure as geopolitical tensions dampened overall risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 MSCI's benchmark emerging stocks index fell 0.4 percent , with the United States and Britain blaming Russia for cyber attacks and the U.S. accusing Russia or Syria of blocking international inspectors from reaching the site of a suspected poison gas attack in Syria.\par \par \uc2 Chow said geopolitical events and trade tensions increased the probability of tail risk events that could harm global activity and emerging market exports, and were making investors cautious.\par \par \uc2 "But they don't alter the central scenario, which is that emerging market growth is still pretty solid and improving," he added, flagging China's continued resilience.\par \par \uc2 China's economy grew by 6.8 percent in the first quarter of 2018 from a year earlier, unchanged from the previous quarter, and slightly above expectations.\par \par \uc2 But March industrial output missed expectations and first-quarter fixed-asset investment growth slowed.\par \par \uc2 China's yuan was steady but mainland stocks fell 1.5 percent to near eight-month lows, and Hong Kong shares fell 0.8 percent as trade tensions between China and the U.S. lingered.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Department of Commerce\uc2  has banned U.S. companies from selling components to Chinese telecom equipment maker \uc2 ZTE Corp\uc2  for seven years, U.S. officials said on Monday. ZTE's shares were suspended from trading in Shanghai and Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 In emerging Europe, Turkish stocks led the selling, down 1.3 percent, while the lira weakened 0.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in Asia, the \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as the Hong Kong dollar repeatedly hit the lower end of its allowable trading band.\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  