\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Russia central bank \highlight\uc2  says no plans to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  on rouble\b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2018\par 11:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, background)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, April 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets following a sharp drop in the value of the rouble, playing down the impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of new U.S. sanctions.\par \par \uc2 Volatility on Russian markets has soared since Washington imposed fresh sanctions on April 6, targeting some of Russia's biggest companies and most prominent businessmen to punish Moscow for its alleged meddling in the 2016 U.S. election and other "malign activity".\par \par \uc2 The rouble plunged more than 10 percent versus the dollar last week to its weakest level since late 2016, before recovering slightly to close down 6 percent on the week on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The sharp devaluation prompted market speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would start buying up the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its value, but Deputy Governor Ksenia Yudayeva said on Monday it had no plans to do so.\par \par \uc2 "The situation on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is balanced," she said at a financial conference in Moscow.\par \par \uc2 "We do not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market situation if there is simply volatility on the market or a sharp change in the (rouble) rate, we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if there are risks to financial stability."\par \par \uc2 Yudayeva said the increased market volatility did not currently represent a risk to financial stability and that the situation was more stable than in 2014, when the United States first hit Russia with sanctions over Moscow's role in the Ukraine crisis.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has all the necessary tools to deal with market risks, she added.\par \par \uc2 The promised announcement of yet more U.S. sanctions over Moscow's support for Syrian President \uc2 Bashar al-Assad\uc2  weighed on the rouble and Russian stocks on Monday.\par \par \uc2 At 0925 GMT, the rouble was 0.29 percent weaker against the dollar at 62.22 and had lost 0.48 percent to trade at 76.89 versus the euro.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Elena Fabrichnaya Editing by Jack Stubbs and Catherine Evans) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-4-16T10:48:14.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180416ee4g008he\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
