\par\par \b \uc2 HSBC\uc2  Turns 'Mildly Bullish' on Inflation-Linked Bonds -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2018\par 12:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1022 GMT - \uc2 HSBC\uc2  shifts to "mildly bullish" from "neutral" on inflation-linked bonds, says rates strategist Theologis Chapsalis. Carry turns positive for both eurozone and U.K. linkers in April, "so investors are enticed to increase their inflation-linked allocations." Italy and France have already responded to this demand by launching new inflation-linked bonds in the last week of March. Chapsalis says the mix of higher headline HICPx [HICP ex-tobacco] and softer core inflation is "particularly favorable" for eurolinkers as it leads to higher carry while providing ammunition for the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be dovish. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 1008 GMT - With the Russian ruble continuing to fall, there is a "small ray of hope for the RUB," which could "come from oil prices after Saudi voiced its support to keep brent crude closer to $80 a barrel in 2019," says \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  . However, "it is too soon to call the all-clear" in the Russian ruble downturn until there is greater certainty over how the U.S. will respond to the chemical attack in Syria. The current levels of the Russian ruble are "attractive" though, SocGen says. USD/RUB last up 1.7% at 64.2572, having reached its highest since late 2016 at 64.7350, according to Factset.(olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0953 GMT - The Russian ruble continues to fall on Wednesday, with USD/RUB up 1.2% at 63.9460, but until USD/RUB gets closer to 75, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  . "This is still around 16% away from the current spot level, and it would require large institutional outflows to get there," SocGen says. But "large flows have not yet been identified," SocGen adds. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0942 GMT - As the euro rises after \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  member \uc2 Ewald Nowotny\uc2  said he had no problem with increasing the deposit rate from -0.4% to -0.2%, \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  reiterates that the euro appreciation is "fragile," keeping its forecast of "downside pressure" on EUR/USD over the coming months. "The more the market is concentrating on EUR positive news right now, the higher the potential for disappointments for the euro if the \uc2 ECB\uc2  back paddles," it says. EUR/USD is last up 0.1% to 1.2370, partially due to some dollar weakness. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0905 GMT - Taiwan's inflationary pressure is on the rise and together with an improving economy it will create a window of opportunity for normalizing monetary policy, says \uc2 BofA Merrill Lynch\uc2 . March inflation eased to 1.6% from a 2.2% seasonal spike in February, but still pushed up the average for the year so far. The bank expects the pace of price growth will more than double from last year's average of 0.6%. Still, the potential spread of US trade protectionism and strained cross-strait relations could pose headwinds to the exports sector and lower the probability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raising rates this year, it adds.(chester.yung@wsj.com;@chester_yung)\par \par \uc2 0854 GMT - The U.K. industrial production rose by 0.1% month-on-month in February, a much weaker increase compared with January and compared with the consensus in a WSJ poll. Sterling falls only slightly on the news, given that further data showed the U.K. trade deficit shrank to GBP10.2 billion in February. GBP/USD falls slightly to 1.4195 from 1.4209 beforehand, but this still leaves it up by 0.1% and not far from an earlier two-week high of 1.4224. EUR/GBP rises to 0.8718, from 0.8703 previously. Manufacturing production fell 0.2% in February, compared with a 0.1% rise in the previous month. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0849 GMT - U.K. factory output declined in February, the latest sign the economy slowed in the first quarter. Manufacturing output fell 0.2%, though overall industrial production recorded a 0.1% gain, thanks largely to higher energy generation as Britons nudged up the thermostat during a cold snap, the \uc2 Office for National Statistics\uc2  says. Most forecasters expect the U.K. to lag its peers for a second year during 2018 as uncertainty over the country's future ties to the \uc2 European Union\uc2  weigh on activity. (Jason.Douglas@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0847 GMT - Turkey's current account deficit data in February were slightly better than expectations but still significantly higher year-on-year, taking the 12-month rolling deficit to $53.3 billion, close to 6% of GDP, says Tim Ash of \uc2 Bluebay Asset Management\uc2  . He notes that portfolio flows saw outflows for February of $227 million, after a net inflow of $5 billion in January. He says the reversal of portfolio inflows is a concern, as they have been funding half the current account deficit. If they reverse this could spell double trouble for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "This release just affirms the vulnerabilities on the BOP [balance of payments] front for Turkey, and underlines the challenges for the \uc2 CBRT\uc2  in managing the lira when Erdogan has tied both hands behind its back in terms of limiting its ability to hike policy rates," Ash says. USD/TRY is last up 0.6% at 4.1437. (yeliz.candemir@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0845 GMT - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator hints it might give domestic fund managers more leeway to invest in international stocks and bonds. Some in the market see the trial balloon as a potential tactic by Beijing to signal its willingness to open up its markets amid trade tensions with the US. The \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator said it "welcome[s] everyone to pay attention" to its statement at the end of this month on the Qualified Domestic Institutional Investor. That's a long-existing program which lets Chinese asset managers put money to work overseas. But the total has been capped at around $90 billion since early 2015 as the government has tried to cap overall outflows from China. The regulator's statement today stopped short of saying it would boost quotas. (chao.deng@wsj.com; @chao_deng)\par \par \uc2 0839 GMT - The Polish zloty could fall after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision on Wednesday, but ING says "any negative impact on PLN" is likely "to be short-lived." It advises to "fade any move in EUR/PLN above 4.20." EUR/PLN is last up by 0.1% at 4.1921. The \uc2 National Bank of Poland\uc2  is likely to "reaffirm its dovish rhetoric, especially after a very soft CPI inflation reading in March," says ING, adding that at "the press conference, Governor Glapi\u324\'01\'44ski is likely to confirm that interest rates hikes are unnecessary in the low inflation environment." ING forecasts EUR/PLN at 4.10 in six months.(olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0833 GMT - India's securitization market is set to get deeper with the country's 1st deal backed by lease receivables on smartphones. OPC Asset Solutions, a private lease/rental company, plans to raise INR50 billion ($766 million) from an up-to-3-year deal that will mostly be sold to mutual-fund investors. \uc2 OPC\uc2  gets lease income from \uc2 Reliance Retail\uc2  for smartphones used by upstart \uc2 Reliance Jio\uc2  's customers. Both are controlled by \uc2 Mukesh Ambani\uc2  , who heads India's largest private sector company--\uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  . (manju.dalal@wsj.com; @manjudalalsg)\par \par \uc2 0821 GMT - The former leader of the \uc2 WTO\uc2  doesn't get Trump on trade. His views are "very different" from what most people believe in, \uc2 Pascal Lamy\uc2  contended at the \uc2 Boao Forum\uc2  in Hainan. He added the President believes at the same time that imports to the US are bad while exports are great. "To be frank, I don't understand what is the purpose of Mr. Trump. I doubt whether we live on the same trade planet." (lin.zhu@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 11, 2018 06:22 ET (10:22 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180411ee4b000zd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
