\par\par \b \uc2 Russian Ruble Volatility May Translate into Global Market Unrest: BNY Mellon -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2018\par 15:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0923 ET - BNY Mellon advises keeping a close eye on Russian stock and bond markets and the Russian ruble after U.S. imposed new sanctions, because "volatility in the RUB has often coincided with broader global market unrest." The ruble wasn't always the causal factor, but "it certainly was a significant influence both in 1998," when the Russian government devalued the ruble, and in late 2014, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would allow the ruble to trade freely. "If you take the history of the last 20 years where there has been unrest on Russian markets it has fed through into broader uncertainty," says Simon Derrick, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNY Mellon. USD/RUB is last up 2.1% at 64.4905. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0847 ET - \uc2 US government\uc2  bond prices rose after data showed consumer prices fell in March, easing investor concerns that inflation could be picking up. The yield on the benchmark 10-year \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  note was recently at 2.765%, compared with 2.799% Tuesday. Yields came under pressure earlier as threats from President Trump to Russia that US missiles "will be coming" to Syria push US stock futures lower. (akane.otani@wsj.com; @akaneotani)\par \par \uc2 0846 ET - Healthy demand is expected to emerge for Italy's offer of the 30-year government bond, the 3.45% March 2048 BTP, at Thursday's auction, given the still relatively high yield, says \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  . Luca Cazzulani, deputy head of fixed income strategy, expects investors' interest for this part of the yield curve to be healthy. The March 2048 BTP is trading at a yield of 2.87%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . The current market level is below the 3.16% allotment yield at the last auction of this BTP in mid-February. However, the current level is "still relatively close to the 3% mark," Cazzulani says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0844 ET - The core consumer price index measure has been tempered in the past year largely because of declines in cell phone plan prices seen at the beginning of 2017. Last month's annual measure of core price growth wiped out that effect, now that it's been a year since the major cell plan price drop, with prices increasing at their strongest pace in about a year. (sharon.nunn@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0842 ET - Real average weekly earnings increased 0.4% in March because of an increase in hourly earnings and because hours worked remained unchanged. Workers saw the increase in hourly earnings because of a 0.3% on-the-month pay bump and a 0.1% decline in the consumer price index that made goods cheaper. (sharon.nunn@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0840 ET - The Consumer Price Index declined 0.1% in March from the previous month, the first monthly decline since May of last year, the Labor Department says. A sharp drop in the gas index outweighed increases in prices for shelter, medical care and food, dragging the overall headline index down. Still, prices increased 2.4% in March from the prior year, the largest jump in a year. Meanwhile, when stripping the volatile food and energy components, the index increased 0.2% on the month and 2.1% on the year, the largest annual gain in a little more than a year. Inflation popped last month, gas prices are just hiding the underlying price growth. (sharon.nunn@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0815 ET - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be less willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the fall of the Russian ruble after the "heavy drain" in Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves during the 2014 crisis, according to BNY Mellon. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of a new fiscal rule, is currently buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the extra cash from oil revenues. Moreover, BNY Mellon says that "Economy Minister \uc2 Maxim Oreshkin\uc2  implied exactly...that the floating RUB would help to mitigate the impact of new U.S. sanctions on the Russian economy." USD/RUB last up 2.3% at 64.6068, EUR/RUB up 2.5% at 80.0004.(olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0813 ET - Quarterly U.K. GDP growth slowed to 0.2% in the first quarter of 2018 from 0.4% in 4Q, following weaker-than-expected U.K. industrial production data, says the National Institute of Economic and Social Research (NIESR). "The main reason for the weakness was severe weather in March, which is likely to have disrupted activity," though poor weather can sometimes result in data revisions, says \uc2 Amit Kara\uc2  , head of U.K. macroeconomic forecasting at NIESR. According to earlier figures, U.K. industrial output rose 0.1% on month in February. Sterling turns lower on the day against the dollar, last at 1.4165, down from 1.4196 before NIESR's announcement. EUR/GBP up 0.2% at 0.8739.\par \par \uc2 (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0813 ET - The fall in the Russian ruble is likely to continue, given that USD/RUB is "being used as a hedge vehicle by bond investors," who until now have been mostly long the Russian ruble, says ING. Falls could be offset by capital flows, however. "RUB high carry status and likely capital repatriation by major Russian businessmen, oligarchs and wealthy individuals may offset or, at least, ease the negative pressure from financial investors selling RUB now," ING says.USD/RUB rises 2.3% to its highest in more than 16 months at 65.0359, according to Factset. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0805 ET - The latest sanctions on Russia have created a "precedent which could be used against any Russian company without clear and transparent arguments," says ING. This increases the risks of further sanctions, it says. "Investors may try to limit exposure to Russian stocks and bonds" as a result. "The same arguments work for foreign banks working in Russia--mostly European, not the U.S. banks--exposing them to potential losses via direct profit and loss effects, and a loss of future business," ING adds. USD/RUB is last up 2.2% at 64.5641. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0754 ET - The indirect effects of U.S. sanctions on Russian oligarchs and their public companies may be more important, given that the direct impact of the actual sanctions on the Russian economy "doesn't look too biting," says ING. "Non-U.S. entities may start behaving in a way that poses additional restrictions not stated in the official sanction wording." There may appear some "defending strategies used by global banks' compliance/legal departments," which would create another layer of self-made sanctions from global banks and financial firms, ING says. The fall in the Russian ruble continues for a third consecutive day, with USD/RUB rising to its highest in more than 16 months at 64.0359 and EUR/RUB reaching a 2-year high of 80.4986, according to Factset. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0725 ET - \uc2 HSBC\uc2  remains "mildly bearish" on core eurozone bonds, like Germany, anticipating falling prices and rising yields. This view is based on the prospect of an end to the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's net asset purchases pulling 10-year core yields higher, says \uc2 HSBC\uc2  rates strategist Wilson Chin. \uc2 HSBC\uc2  maintains its call for a year-end level in 10-year German bund yields of 0.90%, despite the recent fall in core rates, Chin says. The 10-year Bund yield last trades at a yield of 0.49%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 11, 2018 09:23 ET (13:23 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180411ee4b001ue\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
