\par\par \b \uc2 Weekly Earnings Jump On Higher Pay, Lower Costs -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2018\par 14:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0842 ET - Real average weekly earnings increased 0.4% in March because of an increase in hourly earnings and because hours worked remained unchanged. Workers saw the increase in hourly earnings because of a 0.3% on-the-month pay bump and a 0.1% decline in the consumer price index that made goods cheaper. (sharon.nunn@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0840 ET - The Consumer Price Index declined 0.1% in March from the previous month, the first monthly decline since May of last year, the Labor Department says. A sharp drop in the gas index outweighed increases in prices for shelter, medical care and food, dragging the overall headline index down. Still, prices increased 2.4% in March from the prior year, the largest jump in a year. Meanwhile, when stripping the volatile food and energy components, the index increased 0.2% on the month and 2.1% on the year, the largest annual gain in a little more than a year. Inflation popped last month, gas prices are just hiding the underlying price growth. (sharon.nunn@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0815 ET - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be less willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the fall of the Russian ruble after the "heavy drain" in Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves during the 2014 crisis, according to BNY Mellon. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as part of a new fiscal rule, is currently buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the extra cash from oil revenues. Moreover, BNY Mellon says that "Economy Minister \uc2 Maxim Oreshkin\uc2  implied exactly...that the floating RUB would help to mitigate the impact of new U.S. sanctions on the Russian economy." USD/RUB last up 2.3% at 64.6068, EUR/RUB up 2.5% at 80.0004.(olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0813 ET - Quarterly U.K. GDP growth slowed to 0.2% in the first quarter of 2018 from 0.4% in 4Q, following weaker-than-expected U.K. industrial production data, says the National Institute of Economic and Social Research (NIESR). "The main reason for the weakness was severe weather in March, which is likely to have disrupted activity," though poor weather can sometimes result in data revisions, says \uc2 Amit Kara\uc2  , head of U.K. macroeconomic forecasting at NIESR. According to earlier figures, U.K. industrial output rose 0.1% on month in February. Sterling turns lower on the day against the dollar, last at 1.4165, down from 1.4196 before NIESR's announcement. EUR/GBP up 0.2% at 0.8739.\par \par \uc2 (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0813 ET - The fall in the Russian ruble is likely to continue, given that USD/RUB is "being used as a hedge vehicle by bond investors," who until now have been mostly long the Russian ruble, says ING. Falls could be offset by capital flows, however. "RUB high carry status and likely capital repatriation by major Russian businessmen, oligarchs and wealthy individuals may offset or, at least, ease the negative pressure from financial investors selling RUB now," ING says.USD/RUB rises 2.3% to its highest in more than 16 months at 65.0359, according to Factset. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0805 ET - The latest sanctions on Russia have created a "precedent which could be used against any Russian company without clear and transparent arguments," says ING. This increases the risks of further sanctions, it says. "Investors may try to limit exposure to Russian stocks and bonds" as a result. "The same arguments work for foreign banks working in Russia--mostly European, not the U.S. banks--exposing them to potential losses via direct profit and loss effects, and a loss of future business," ING adds. USD/RUB is last up 2.2% at 64.5641. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0754 ET - The indirect effects of U.S. sanctions on Russian oligarchs and their public companies may be more important, given that the direct impact of the actual sanctions on the Russian economy "doesn't look too biting," says ING. "Non-U.S. entities may start behaving in a way that poses additional restrictions not stated in the official sanction wording." There may appear some "defending strategies used by global banks' compliance/legal departments," which would create another layer of self-made sanctions from global banks and financial firms, ING says. The fall in the Russian ruble continues for a third consecutive day, with USD/RUB rising to its highest in more than 16 months at 64.0359 and EUR/RUB reaching a 2-year high of 80.4986, according to Factset. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0725 ET - \uc2 HSBC\uc2  remains "mildly bearish" on core eurozone bonds, like Germany, anticipating falling prices and rising yields. This view is based on the prospect of an end to the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's net asset purchases pulling 10-year core yields higher, says \uc2 HSBC\uc2  rates strategist Wilson Chin. \uc2 HSBC\uc2  maintains its call for a year-end level in 10-year German bund yields of 0.90%, despite the recent fall in core rates, Chin says. The 10-year Bund yield last trades at a yield of 0.49%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  . (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0719 ET - Turkey is witnessing a vicious cycle of a weaker lira undermining confidence amongst investors, as reflected in the sharp fall in Turkish stocks and bonds, says \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  . "This in turn could trigger substantial capital outflows and lead to even stronger selling pressure on the lira," it says. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could stop or at least slow this vicious cycle or at least can slow it down by raising interest rates on April 25. However, this "would be an unpopular decision amongst prominent Turkish officials, who are in favour of preserving robust economic growth ahead of crucial elections next year," says \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  . USD/TRY last up 1.4% at 4.1687, having hit a record high of 4.1735, according to Factset.(yeliz.candemir@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0648 ET - Some media reports that the U.S. may be thinking of imposing further sanctions on Russia after the chemical attack in Syria prompt \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  to warn of a "risk of further ruble depreciation." USD/RUB continues to fall on Wednesday, with USD/RUB up 1.5% at 64.0937, having reached its highest in more than 16 months at 64.7350, according to Factset. "In the current uncertain situation, we think the RUB will likely remain under pressure," \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  says. The ruble has dropped to a string of multi-month lows this week.(olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 0622 ET - \uc2 HSBC\uc2  shifts to "mildly bullish" from "neutral" on inflation-linked bonds, says rates strategist Theologis Chapsalis. Carry turns positive for both eurozone and U.K. linkers in April, "so investors are enticed to increase their inflation-linked allocations." Italy and France have already responded to this demand by launching new inflation-linked bonds in the last week of March. Chapsalis says the mix of higher headline HICPx [HICP ex-tobacco] and softer core inflation is "particularly favorable" for eurolinkers as it leads to higher carry while providing ammunition for the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be dovish. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0608 ET - With the Russian ruble continuing to fall, there is a "small ray of hope for the RUB," which could "come from oil prices after Saudi voiced its support to keep brent crude closer to $80 a barrel in 2019," says \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  . However, "it is too soon to call the all-clear" in the Russian ruble downturn until there is greater certainty over how the U.S. will respond to the chemical attack in Syria. The current levels of the Russian ruble are "attractive" though, SocGen says. USD/RUB last up 1.7% at 64.2572, having reached its highest since late 2016 at 64.7350, according to Factset.(olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 11, 2018 08:42 ET (12:42 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180411ee4b001pv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
