\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russia cuts main interest rate, aims to complete easing cycle by end of 2018\b0\par\par\uc2 651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2018\par 17:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cuts benchmark rate by 25 bps to 7.25 pct\par \par \uc2 * Says plans to complete easing cycle with more cuts this year\par \par \uc2 * Says trade protectionism has had little impact on Russia so far\par \par \uc2 * Rouble shows muted reaction to the priced-in rate move (Adds quotes, detail)\par \par \uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh and Jack Stubbs\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 23 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its main interest rate by 25 basis points on Friday and said it expects to complete a cycle of monetary easing this year, although global trade protectionism remains a risk.\par \par \uc2 Russia needs lower interest rates to prop up a stalling economic recovery through cheaper lending, and lower inflation means it can reduce rates more.\par \par \uc2 In its second rate cut so far in 2018, the bank lowered its benchmark rate to 7.25 percent from 7.50 percent, matching market expectations.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began reducing rates soon after an emergency hike to 17 percent in late 2014 aimed at shielding the economy as the value of the rouble plunged and Western economic sanctions over Moscow's actions in Ukraine took their toll.\par \par \uc2 Since then, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has managed to rein in inflation, once stuck in double digits, bringing it down to a record low of 2.2 percent in February.\par \par \uc2 Inflation has slowed to below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ultimate target of 4 percent, giving the bank room to cut its main rate until it settles somewhere in the 6-7 percent range it sees as roughly "neutral".\par \par \uc2 "We see that a potential for lowering the key rate exists now. We expect to complete the switch to neutral monetary policy this year," \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Elvira Nabiullina\uc2  said at a news conference.\par \par \uc2 Nabiullina said a pause in the rate-cutting cycle should not be ruled out but policy will remain predictable and any changes will be gradual.\par \par \uc2 The former economy minister also said risks of trade protectionism have increased globally, but she added that the direct impact on the Russian economy had been limited so far.\par \par \uc2 Asked if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could resume buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , something it last did in 2015, Nabiullina said \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international reserves could approach $500 billion without \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Analysts at Renaissance Capital said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was now in a "dovish phase" of the easing cycle and its rhetoric might change if inflation picks up faster than previously thought.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  analysts noted that the bank's estimated neutral rate of 6-7 percent meant it could cut by anything from 25 to 125 basis points more.\par \par \uc2 "But, when questioned about what was likely, Ms. Nabiullina sounded deliberately vague," they added in a note to investors.\par \par \uc2 Steady and low inflation reduces uncertainty for businesses and is important for households too, Nabiullina said, adding that all this together should contribute to stronger economic growth in Russia.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated its gross domestic product growth forecast for 2018 of 1.5-2.0 percent, saying it expects inflation to bounce off historic lows in the second quarter and rise towards its target of 4 percent later this year.\par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Russia's general perceptions of the Russian economy's growth have remained unchanged," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Friday's rate cut was widely priced in as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's head of monetary policy had said earlier this month that he would recommend lowering the rate further.\par \par \uc2 The rouble showed muted reaction to the rate move, firming slightly to 57.12 versus the dollar as of 1437 GMT compared with 57.21 shortly before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement.\par \par \uc2 The bank's board next meets on April 27. (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh and Jack Stubbs Editing by Hugh Lawson) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-3-23T17:06:54.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180323ee3n00fl6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
