\par\par \b \uc2 Press Release: \uc2 Fitch\uc2 : Russian Bank Sector Stable Despite Private Bank Failures\b0\par\par\uc2 1,590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2018\par 15:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par The following is a press release from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  : \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Link to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  ' Report(s): What Investors Want to Know: Russian Banks\f28 \par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/10021425"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/10021425 }}}\par \par \uc2 - Fitch Ratings -Moscow-02 March 2018: \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  says in a new report that the Russian banking sector remains stable despite the recent failures of several large privately-owned banks, as swift \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 CBR\uc2 ) prevented losses for senior creditors and limited contagion. Any further high-profile bank failures in 2018 are unlikely to rival last year's in scale and should not be a source of broader risks for the system.\par \par \uc2 We see the main near-term risks for the sector as increasing competition, which will force weaker players to go out of business, and relaxation of retail underwriting (extension of loan tenors and reduction of rates), coupled with increasing borrower leverage. More broadly, a potential fall in oil prices and the resulting economic decline would be negative for banks, as would further sanctions, which, in an extreme scenario could result in a weakening of the sovereign's propensity to support foreign creditors of state-owned banks.\par \par \uc2 In 2018-2019, we expect modest lending growth of about 5% a year, while return on equity should remain reasonable at about 15%, as lower provisioning charges will be offset by lower margins. The longer-term performance of the economy and the banking system will depend significantly on oil prices and geopolitical developments.\par \par \uc2 The Special Report, "What Investors Want to Know: Russian Banks", is available at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.fitchratings.com}}}\uc2  or by clicking on the link above, and has been published on the back of more than 40 recent meetings with emerging-market fixed-income investors.\par \par \uc2 Contact:\par \par \uc2 Alexander Danilov\par \par \uc2 - Senior Director\par \par \uc2 - +7 495 956 2408\par \par \uc2 - Fitch Ratings Moscow\par \par \uc2 - 26 Valovaya Street\par \par \uc2 - Moscow 115054\par \par \uc2 James Watson, CFA\par \par \uc2 - Managing Director\par \par \uc2 - +7 495 956 6657\par \par \uc2 Media Relations: Julia Belskaya von Tell, Moscow, Tel: +7 495 956 9908, Email: julia.belskayavontell@fitchratings.com; Peter Fitzpatrick, London, Tel: +44 20 3530 1103, Email: peter.fitzpatrick@fitchratings.com.\par \par \uc2 Additional information is available on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.fitchratings.com}}}\par \par \uc2 ALL FITCH CREDIT RATINGS ARE SUBJECT TO CERTAIN LIMITATIONS AND DISCLAIMERS. PLEASE READ THESE LIMITATIONS AND DISCLAIMERS BY FOLLOWING THIS LINK: HTTPS://WWW.FITCHRATINGS.COM/UNDERSTANDINGCREDITRATINGS. IN ADDITION, RATING DEFINITIONS AND THE TERMS OF USE OF SUCH RATINGS ARE AVAILABLE ON THE AGENCY'S PUBLIC WEB SITE AT WWW.FITCHRATINGS.COM. PUBLISHED RATINGS, CRITERIA, AND METHODOLOGIES ARE AVAILABLE FROM THIS SITE AT ALL TIMES. FITCH'S CODE OF CONDUCT, CONFIDENTIALITY, CONFLICTS OF INTEREST, AFFILIATE FIREWALL, COMPLIANCE, AND OTHER RELEVANT POLICIES AND PROCEDURES ARE ALSO AVAILABLE FROM THE CODE OF CONDUCT SECTION OF THIS SITE. DIRECTORS AND SHAREHOLDERS RELEVANT INTER