\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia and Venezuela must sign on Wednesday a restructuring of debt\b0\par\par\uc2 479 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2017\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Russia and Venezuela, the latter declared by a partial default financial rating agency, must sign on Wednesday an agreement to restructure 3,000 million dollars in debt Caracas contracted with Moscow, reported different sources Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The firm is scheduled on Wednesday, a source close to the Russian Government told AFP.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  Russian refused to confirm this information and does not provide any public event.\par \par \uc2 Without confirming the date of signature, the Embassy of Venezuela in Moscow announced a press conference on Wednesday, November 15 "to report on the signing of agreements on the restructuring of the Venezuelan debt with Russia".\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  Russian announced last week that Venezuela had given his agreement to restructure its debt with Russia according to the modalities agreed between the two countries, without specifying what.\par \par \uc2 Carlos Far\u237\'00\'EDa, Venezuelan Ambassador to Russia, had stated that the signing of an agreement between the two countries should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  before November 15.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and China are the two main creditors and allies of Venezuela, who owes them respectively 8.000 and 28,000 million dollars.\par \par \uc2 In October, Russian Finance Minister \uc2 Anton Siluanov\uc2 , had told the Interfax agency that the agreement provided for separate payments in two stages, with a first "a small amount" with "quite favorable conditions", so Venezuela can "transfer the" most"debt in a second stage.\par \par \uc2 But, in total, the debt of Venezuela with Russia is more important, counting the 6,000 million dollars owed oil company \uc2 PDVSA\uc2  to the semi-public Russian group Rosneft.\par \par \uc2 Of these, 2,500 million were paid between may 2016 and 2017 April in the form of advance by contracts for deliveries of oil and fuel provided to 2019.\par \par \uc2 Some experts interpreted these payments as a financial support concealed to Caracas.\par \par \uc2 In a press conference call, the first Vice-President of Rosneft, \uc2 Pavel Fedorov\uc2 , said on Tuesday that there was "no risk of default" by \uc2 PDVSA\uc2 , which would effect "all payments in accordance with the agreed timetable".\par \par \uc2 The financial rating agency Standard & Poors said on Tuesday to Venezuela in "partial default" after missing a payment of 200 million dollars in bonds and a few hours after two meetings of creditors on Monday in Caracas and New York.\par \par \uc2 "We have lowered two ratings to '' (default), and down the rating of long-term foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sovereign debt to 'SD' (partial default)," said S & P.\par \par \uc2 S & P said to have taken such a decision within a grace period of 30 days for the payment of obligations.\par \par \uc2 Venezuela, drowned out by the economic crisis, wants to restructure its foreign debt, estimated at 150,000 million dollars. It would only have reserves for 9,700 million and should repay bonds for at least 1,470 billion before year's end and 8,000 million in 2018.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020171114edbe002qd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
