\par\par \b \uc2 *Fitch Downgrades \uc2 Uraltransbank\uc2  to 'CCC'; On RWN\b0\par\par\uc2 1,806 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 2017\par 17:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 2 Jun 2017 11:00 ET  Press Release: Fitch Downgrades \uc2 Uraltransbank\uc2  to 'CCC'; On RWN\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par The following is a press release from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2 : \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2 -Moscow/London-02 June 2017: \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  has downgraded \uc2 Uraltransbank\uc2 's (UTB) Long-Term Issuer Default Rating (IDR) to 'CCC' from 'B-' and placed it on Rating Watch Negative (RWN). A full list of rating actions is at the end of this commentary.\par \par \uc2 KEY RATING DRIVERS\par \par \uc2 - The downgrade of UTB's IDR to 'CCC' and RWN mainly reflect the fact that the bank breached the Tier 1 minimum capital requirement in April, which according to Russian legislation, could lead to a regulatory \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . According to management, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (CBR) has provided forbearance by giving the bank until end-August to improve its capital position.\par \par \uc2 UTB plans to do this by selling some problem loan exposures above the net value. However, in Fitch's view, there is significant near-term uncertainty with respect to UTB's ability to sustainably restore compliance, given the bank's somewhat optimistic assumptions around the planned problem loan sale, its continuously loss-making performance and weak asset quality.\par \par \uc2 The bank's Tier 1 capital ratio dropped to 5.3% (minimum 6%, 7.3% with buffers) at end-4M17 from 7.6% at end-2016 due to RUB200 million losses from year end. Core Tier 1 (5.3%; minimum 4.5%) and total capital (9%; 8% minimum) ratios were above the minimum at end-4M17, but cushions were only modest. Fitch Core Capital (\uc2 FCC\uc2 ) ratio was stronger at 13.1% at end-2016 as IFRS risk-weighted assets are 35% lower, mostly due to significant operating risk component and different weightings of loans under regulatory rules.\par \par \uc2 UTB expects to sell few large problem exposures to a third party before end-August above the net value releasing RUB200 million-RUB250 million of provisions. If successful, the Tier 1 ratio should improve to 7.0%-7.5%. However, UTB's capitalisation will remain under pressure due to weak asset quality (NPLs including full-recourse overdue loans transferred to collection agencies stood at 32%, but were fully reserved, while NPL origination ratio was 6% in 2016) and performance (it lost 15% of equity in 4M17).\par \par \uc2 Liquidity is currently good (liquid assets covered high 55% of customer accounts at end-4M17), but may come under pressure if depositors become increasingly concerned with the bank's viability prospects following the capital requirements breach.\par \par \uc2 The Support Rating of '5' and Support Rating Floor of 'No Floor' reflects the bank's small size and limited franchise, making extraordinary capital support from the state, in case of need, unlikely.\par \par \uc2 RATING SENSITIVITIES\par \par \uc2 - Fitch will resolve the RWN and downgrade the ratings if the bank is unable to return to compliance with capital requirements leading to CBR \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 UTB's IDRs could stabilise at their current levels, or ultimately be upgraded back to 'B-' if the bank is able to rebuild its capital and improve performance.\par \par \uc2 -\par \par \uc2 - The rating actions are as follows:\par \par \uc2 Long-Term Foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: downgraded to 'CCC' from'B-;' placed on RWN\par \par \uc2 - Short-Term Foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: downgraded to 'C' from 'B'; placed on RWN\par \par \uc2 - Viability Rating: downgraded to 'ccc' from 'b-'; placed on RWN\par \par \uc2 - Support Rating: affirmed at '5'\par \par \uc2 - Support Rating Floor affirmed at 'No Floor'\par \par \uc2 Contact:\par \par \uc2 - Primary Analyst\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Anton Lopatin\par \par \uc2 - Director\par \par \uc2 - +7 495 956 7096\par \par \uc2 - Fitch Ratings CIS Ltd\par \par \uc2 - 26 Valovaya Street,\par \par \uc2 - Moscow 115054\par \par \uc2 Secondary Analyst\par \par \uc2 - Konstantin Alekseenko\par \par \uc2 - Analyst\par \par \uc2 - +7 495 956 2401\par \par \uc2 Committee Chairperson\par \par \uc2 - Olga Ignatieva\par \par \uc2 - Senior Director\par \par \uc2 - +7 495 956 6906\par \par \uc2 Media Relations: Julia Belskaya von Tell, Moscow, Tel: +7 495 956 9908, Email: julia.belskayavontell@fitchratings.com; Peter Fitzpatrick, London, Tel: +44 20 3530 1103, Email: peter.fitzpatrick@fitchratings.com.\par \par \uc2 Additional information is available on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.fitchratings.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Applicable Criteria\par \par \uc2 - Global Bank Rating Criteria (pub. 25 Nov 2016)\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/891051"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.fitchratings.com/site/re/891051}}}\par \par \uc2 Additional Disclosures\par \par \uc2 - Dodd-Frank Rating Information Disclosure Form\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/site/dodd-frank-disclosure/1024606"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.fitchratings.com/site/dodd-frank-disclosure/1024606}}}\par \par \uc2 - Solicitation Status\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/site/pr/1024606#solicitation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.fitchratings.com/site/pr/1024606#solicitation}}}\par \par \uc2 - Endorsement Policy\par \par \uc2 - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fitchratings.com/regulat