\par\par \b \uc2 Russian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  seeks to keep dollar purchase plan at arm's length-sources\b0\par\par\uc2 1,286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2017\par 11:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (The following is an updated version of a Thursday report, adding Friday's finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcements)\par \par \uc2 * Rouble to feel extra pressure as cbank returns to market\par \par \uc2 * Cbank was reluctant to resume \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  - sources\par \par \uc2 * Plan to rebuild fiscal buffers finds support in Kremlin\par \par \uc2 * Rouble seen 10 pct weaker at $55 oil under new budget rule\par \par \uc2 * GRAPHIC - Rouble and oil prices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2kg8djk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2kg8djk}}}\par \par \uc2 By Darya Korsunskaya and Andrey Ostroukh\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Feb 3 (Reuters) - Russia will resume buying dollars next week for the first time since a brief burst in 2015, but sources told Reuters the purchases will go ahead only after a reluctant \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won assurances it could distance itself from the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 People involved in discussions of the planned purchases said the bank had feared investors would regard them as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  designed to weaken the rouble, rather than the stated intention of replenishing Russia's fiscal reserves depleted by low oil prices and international sanctions.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has a policy of letting the rouble float freely, insists it is not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate. Instead, it said last month that it would merely buy the dollars on behalf of the finance ministry, which came up with the plan following a modest uptick in oil prices over the past year.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, the purchases may still create a dilemma for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  by putting downward pressure on the rouble after a period of relative calm. Already, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffered its biggest one-day drop so far this year on Jan. 26, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  were announced.\par \par \uc2 The rouble was one of the best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  globally in 2016. However, the government would stand to benefit from a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it means oil revenues earned in dollars would translate into more roubles, allowing it to boost spending. That would be especially helpful in the run-up to elections next year, when President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  is likely to seek a new term.\par \par \uc2 Describing discussions before the announcement between the bank, finance ministry and Kremlin, three sources said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had had misgivings that buying dollars would hurt its reputation on financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Governor Elvira Nabiullina had worried she would have to justify the new round of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , one former government official familiar with the matter told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 "But the finance ministry offered a life line by taking responsibility. Now she won't have to answer uneasy questions," said the source. "She will say it was the finance ministry's decision, it's their money, and we are just acting as an operator."\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry announced on Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would buy the equivalent of 6.3 billion roubles ($106 million at current market prices) a day on the Moscow Exchange this month to replenish the country's fiscal reserves.\par \par \uc2 The announcement covers purchases to be made between Feb. 7 and March 6.\par \par \uc2 FACTBOX - Winners and losers from \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it saw less room for interest rate cuts following the announcement of dollar purchases, while keeping the key rate unchanged at 10 percent on Friday.\par \par \uc2 SOBER POLICY-MAKING\par \par \uc2 Many investors credit the bank with steering Russia through an economic crisis since 2014, and view it as a bastion of sober policy-making in an otherwise hard-to-predict Russian system.\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Prime Minister \uc2 Dmitry Medvedev\uc2  said the government has no "levers of pressure" on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said Putin gave no orders to the bank to start dollar buying.\par \par \uc2 The bank last bought dollars on the domestic market in mid-2015 in a short-lived attempt to replenish its reserves, halting them to ease downward pressure on the rouble.\par \par \uc2 Russia's economy was badly hurt by the combined effects of plunging oil prices in 2014-2015 and Western sanctions imposed over the Ukraine crisis. Its Reserve Fund shrank to just $16 billion by early February from nearly $90 billion before Moscow's annexation of Crimea in 2014 as the country spent the money to plug holes in the oil-dependent budget.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  has welcomed the finance ministry plan as it should help to rebuild reserves, improving predictability of fiscal policy. However, it said the budget needed a "more comprehensive oil framework".\par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to keep the purchases at arms' length, it may struggle to dispel the perception of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "This is indeed a step away from a free float. They are doing the right thing, presenting this as an (action by) the finance ministry, not the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a person close to the decision-making process in the Kremlin said.\par \par \uc2 The purchases stem from a budget rule adopted in January. Under this, extra revenues from oil exports would be directed towards rebuilding the Reserve Fund. That means selling roubles on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While from a fiscal point of view that makes sense, according to several economists, it will have a knock-on effect on monetary policy. According to finance ministry projections, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions required to implement the budget rule will push the rouble down.\par \par \uc2 A weaker rouble could increase inflation and thus delay an economic recovery by prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to postpone interest rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 The amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will vary, based on average oil prices in the previous month. The finance ministry will disclose the amount of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  it wants the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy for it at the beginning of every month.\par \par \uc2 ROUBLE FEARS\par \par \uc2 The move to resume dollar purchases came after Finance Minister \uc2 Anton Siluanov\uc2  and Trade Minister \uc2 Denis Manturov\uc2  said Russia was not interested in having a strong rouble.\par \par \uc2 Even though the finance ministry has since presented the budget rule as a measure to limit the economy's dependence on oil prices, its appearance shortly after the rouble had firmed to its strongest since July 2015 fuelled speculation that its real goal was to restrain the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Both the timing and ad hoc way in which this measure has been implemented will lead many market participants to interpret it more as an attempt at \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  said in a recent research note.\par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  unable to diversify its economy quickly from relying on commodity exports, the budget rule will artificially limit the upside for the rouble as Urals crude <URL-E> remains well above the $40 per barrel price factored into this year's budget planning.\par \par \uc2 If Urals averages $55 - roughly its current level - the budget rule envisages keeping the rouble about 10 percent weaker: the finance ministry sees the dollar at 64.9 roubles under the rule versus 58.05 without the rule. The rouble was around 59.5 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Recent gains in the rouble are harmful to influential exporters who want to receive more roubles for the goods they sell in dollars. On the flip side, a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is better for households and companies operating on the local market as it helps to keep inflation down and makes imports more affordable.\par \par \uc2 Critics say the manner in which the plans for dollar purchases has been executed calls into question the credibility of Russia's monetary and fiscal authorities.\par \par \uc2 "No trust in the rouble will ever emerge if the government devalues the rouble every two years. Manipulations with the exchange rate and monetary policy should not be aimed at solving budget issues," said Pyotr Milovanov, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Metallinvestbank.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Alexander Winning in Moscow and Gwladys Fouche in Oslo; editing by David Stamp)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-2-6T10:59:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170203ed2300i4t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
