\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russian rouble slumps as market frets over  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 707 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2017\par 15:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to start buying \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Feb               \par \par \uc2 * FinMin proposes budget rule to shield economy               \par \par \uc2 * Officials concerned by rouble strength               \par \par \uc2 * Market questions c.bank credibility               \par \par \uc2 * Outlook for c.bank rate cuts now less certain   (Writes through with more detail, comment)               \par \par \uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh and Alexander Winning               \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Jan 26 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble saw its biggest one-day drop so far this year on Thursday, after the finance ministry said it would start buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February as part of an effort to shield the economy from oil price swings.               \par \par \uc2 The purchases are further evidence that officials are more concerned about bolstering public finances than helping out Russian households, which have borne the brunt of an economic slump brought on by weak oil prices.               \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry is considering a budget rule that would limit spending from Russia's fiscal reserves if the price of Urals crude oil <URL-E> averages over $40 a barrel, the level used for this year's budget plans. It hopes that will protect the reserves and help curb recent gains by the rouble that have threatened an economic recovery.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which let the rouble float freely in 2014 but will be buying dollars for the finance ministry from February, said the new policy would not contradict the notion of a floating rouble, because the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would serve fiscal rather than monetary purposes.               \par \par \uc2 "There are no grounds for a speculative mood to emerge among market players," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.               \par \par \uc2 The market, however, reacted differently.               \par \par \uc2 Traders had been positioning for \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases since last week, when top officials said following a meeting with President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  that current oil prices meant Russia could buy dollars.               \par \par \uc2 Putin said late last year that something should be done to address the rouble's strengthening, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw some of the largest gains in 2016 among major global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the impact on the rouble was somewhat cushioned by higher global oil prices. But it still saw its biggest one-day fall since late December and traded at 60.44 versus the dollar at 1321 GMT, down 1.6 percent on the day.               \par \par \uc2 The rouble level reflected by three-month non-deliverable forwards was 3 percent weaker than its level on Wednesday, as traders reacted to the announcement on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases.               \par \par \uc2 Forwards showed traders expected the rouble to be at around 61.5 versus the dollar in three months' time and 62.6 in six months' time.                              \par \par \uc2 CREDIBILITY QUESTIONED               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said the upcoming \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases are not intended to affect the rouble. But some market players cautioned the bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would change the balance of power on the market.               \par \par \uc2 "Giving in to the government and buying dollars in large volumes, the Bank of Russia is taking a great risk; trust in its foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is called into question," said Sergei Romanchuk, head of Russia's division of a major \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  industry association, ACI.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  promised to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "evenly" through any given trading session. The amount will correspond to finance ministry calculations disclosed at the beginning of each month.               \par \par \uc2 According to Reuters calculations based on finance ministry documents, the daily purchases may amount to around $130 million should prices for oil blend Urals stay near their current level of $53.3 per barrel.               \par \par \uc2 Citi said it expected daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at just under $100 million per day. Rosbank estimated them at around $90 million.               \par \par \uc2 Sberbank CIB\uc2  analysts said the decision to start buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed the appreciation in the rouble had reached uncomfortable levels for the government, which gets less revenue from exports when the rouble is strong.               \par \par \uc2 They also said it made the outlook for imminent rate cuts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  less certain.               \par \par \uc2 SILVER LINING               \par \par \uc2 The decision to carry out \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases could have positive effects, however.               \par \par \uc2 Protecting its fiscal reserves could help Russia get its sovereign credit ratings upgraded. Lower rouble volatility would make Russian assets even more attractive.               \par \par \uc2 Experts say that while a weaker rouble will make Russian exports more competitive, the effect on inflation could be relatively restrained.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-1-26T15:45:16.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170126ed1q00fdo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
