\par\par \b \uc2 Russian assets recover on expectations of better ties with United States\b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2016\par 08:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 10 (Reuters) - Russian assets rose in early trade on Thursday, lifted by expectations that relations between Moscow and Washington will improve after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the U.S. presidential election.\par \par \uc2 At 0726 GMT, the rouble was 0.7 percent stronger against the dollar at 63.42 and had gained 0.7 percent to trade at 69.29 versus the euro.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was up 1.3 percent at 1,003.6 points, while the rouble-based MICEX was 0.4 percent higher at 2020.0 points.\par \par \uc2 "Some experts had already said earlier that the victory of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  increases the chances for warmer relations between the United States and Russia in the political sphere and in trade and investment," analysts at TeleTrade wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 Trump's victory roiled markets on Wednesday, sending investors scrambling for safe-haven assets such as gold or sovereign bonds. But in the second part of the day markets recovered, quicker than after the Brexit referendum vote in June.\par \par \uc2 Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance ministry officials assuring of a minimal impact from Trump's win also helped, analysts said. Finance Minister \uc2 Anton Siluanov\uc2  said that he expects investors' interest in Russian assets to grow.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices reversed some early losses as markets recovered from their initial shock at Trump's victory, lending further support to Russia's commodity-heavy indexes and the rouble.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, a global benchmark for Russia's main export, was up 0.9 percent at $46.76 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 For rouble poll data see reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 -polls?RIC=RUB=\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 Russia in graphics: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/dun63s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/dun63s}}}\uc2  (Reporting by Lidia Kelly; Editing by Andrey Ostroukh) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-11-10T08:44:29.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020161110ecba00cq5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
