\par\par \b \uc2 Russian rouble steady; falling oil counters Brexit optimism\b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2016\par 09:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, June 21 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble was little changed early on Tuesday as a slight decline in oil prices was countered by risk appetite spurred by polls showing a reduced chance of Britain leaving the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 0739 GMT, the rouble was 0.3 percent stronger against the dollar at 64.11 and had gained less than 0.1 percent to 72.74 versus the euro.\par \par \uc2 The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose on Monday, in line with emerging market peers, as oil prices gained and as fears over Thursday's Brexit referendum eased.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, a global benchmark for Russia's main export, was down 0.6 percent at around $50.4 a barrel on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "If there is a positive outcome of the British referendum, then tactically quite good prospects will open for the rouble," Rosbank analysts said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "Investor interest in the rouble continues to be warmed by the gradual transition of the economy to growth, as well as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lack of intentions to carry out \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy has been in crisis since 2014, when an oil price collapse and Western sanctions over the Ukraine crisis pushed the country into recession. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now expects the economy to show quarterly growth no later than the second half of this year.\par \par \uc2 Russian share indexes were lower on Tuesday, following strong gains on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was down 0.7 percent to 928 points, and the rouble-based MICEX was also 0.7 percent lower at 1,890 points.\par \par \uc2 For rouble poll data see reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 -polls?RIC=RUB=\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 Russia in graphics: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/dun63s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/dun63s}}}\uc2  (Reporting by Alexander Winning, editing by Jason Bush) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-6-21T08:49:24.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160621ec6l00l2d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
