\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Emerging assets extend gains, pinning hopes on G20 action\b0\par\par\uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2016\par 11:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 22 (Reuters) - Emerging stocks rose 0.7 percent on Monday to extend last week's gains, tracking world equity markets higher on expectations of a policy action announcement from the G20 meeting this week.\par \par \uc2 The summit of central bankers and finance ministers from the world's 20 biggest economic powers is likely to include discussions on China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and possible actions that might reassure financial markets and lift global growth.\par \par \uc2 MSCI\uc2 's main emerging equity index has risen 8.5 percent from 6-1/2-year lows hit a month ago, thanks to recent stabilisation on Western stocks, oil producers' efforts to prevent more crude price falls and a pricing out of aggressive U.S. rate rises. The index rose more than 4 percent last week.\par \par \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2 's head of EM strategy Sebastien Barbe said gains were also due to oil prices staying above $30 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 "Of course the G20 may focus a little bit on coordination on the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  side in particular, and also in terms of stimulus, but I would not expect too much from the G20 to be frank as different countries don't always have converging interests," Barbe said.\par \par \uc2 "So I would not bank too much on the G20 to provide lasting support," he said, calling the gains "fragile".\par \par \uc2 Some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially in Asia, are benefiting from tentative stock and bond market inflows. But data is still underscoring emerging economies' slowdown, with South Korean exports shrinking by a sixth versus year-ago levels in the first 20 days of February.\par \par \uc2 The Korean won rose 0.4 percent however on the possibility of more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action following the estimated sale of $2 billion on Friday, and after Mexico's shock \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 In emerging Europe, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rouble rose 1 percent to the dollar, seesawing in line with oil, though local trade was thinned by a public holiday. South Africa's rand rose half a percent, approaching Friday's seven-week highs but with the budget due on Wednesday, further gains looked unlikely.\par \par \uc2 Citi told clients the budget could be a policy turning point for South Africa which risks ratings downgrades to junk status.\par \par \uc2 "At a bare minimum, the market appears to expect four main things: a realistic GDP outlook, expenditure cuts, revenue-raising, and a policy shift (for the better)," Citi said, noting that while a junk rating was likely from S&P in June, fiscal consolidation moves could head off downgrades from Fitch and \uc2 Moody's\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Turkish assets also firmed, with the lira up a quarter percent and stocks rising 1.8 percent to two-week highs . The respite comes after heavy recent losses fuelled by cross-border tensions and a bomb attack in Ankara. However, the country remains one of the most vulnerable emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 In bond news, Peru and Lebanon are gearing up to tap markets, while banks are bidding to run Malaysia's upcoming dollar-denominated sukuk.\par \par \uc2 Emerging dollar bonds' average yield premium over U.S. Treasuries fell under 500 basis points for the first time since early February.\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  performance 2016, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jus35t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jus35t}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on \uc2 MSCI\uc2  emerging index performance 2016, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/weh36s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/weh36s}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on \uc2 MSCI\uc2  emerging Europe performance 2016, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jun28s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jun28s}}}\par \par \uc2 For GRAPHIC on \uc2 MSCI\uc2  frontier index performance 2016, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/zyh97s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/zyh97s}}}\par \par \uc2 For CENTRAL EUROPE market report, see\par \par \uc2 For TURKISH market report, see\par \par \uc2 For RUSSIAN market report, see ) (Additional reporting by Karin Strohecker; Editing by Louise Ireland) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-2-22T11:49:05.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160222ec2m00yhq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
