\par\par \b \uc2 Ruble Falls to Record Low Against the Dollar -- 3rd Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 763 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2016\par 22:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Russian ruble fell to its weakest level ever against the dollar on Thursday even as top officials tried to play down the significance of the depreciation.\par \par \uc2 The ruble hit 86 to the dollar, pressured by weak oil prices, just days after having broken through the psychologically crucial threshold of 80.\par \par \uc2 "Today we saw panic on the Russian market, taking into account that oil prices are almost at yesterday's levels," said Ivan Kopeikin, an expert at BCS Express research firm.\par \par \uc2 The ruble's crash came the day after the Bank of Russia said the depreciation was justified and carried no risks to financial stability. The statement was taken by the market as a direct indication that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no immediate plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the decline in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't supported the ruble since late 2014. It let the ruble float freely from Nov. 10 of that year and eliminated regular \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after spending several dozen billions of dollars from its reserves. Since then the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if there are risks to financial stability.\par \par \uc2 In this latest ruble relapse, the Kremlin's spokesman \uc2 Dmitry Peskov\uc2  also acted as if the drop to all-time lows was a normal development.\par \par \uc2 "I wouldn't use the word collapse. The exchange rate is really changing, the rate is volatile, but it's far from collapsing," Mr. Peskov said Thursday, Russian news agencies reported.\par \par \uc2 In response to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's and the Kremlin's reaction, the market concluded that worse is ahead, said Natalia Orlova, economist at Alfa Bank.\par \par \uc2 The drop in the ruble on Thursday was exacerbated by technical factors, such as margin calls and stop losses, after the dollar rose above its previous all-time high of 80.1 rubles seen at the peak of financial crisis in 2014, market players said.\par \par \uc2 In evening trade on the Moscow exchange, the ruble lost nearly 3% of its value, trading at 83.8 against the greenback. This is 12% weaker than in late 2015 and 22% weaker than a year ago.\par \par \uc2 The ruble's weakness carries inflationary risks, which may limit the room for monetary easing needed to limit economic contraction. Many people view the ruble's depreciation as a sign that consumer prices will rise, said Marina Krasilnikova, an expert the independent pollster Levada Center.\par \par \uc2 Given the increasing inflationary risks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to keep the key rate unchanged at 11% when it holds its next board meeting on Jan. 29, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 Some recovery in the ruble is likely in the near term. Export-focused companies usually support the ruble at the end of every month by converting their dollars and euro revenues to meet local month-end taxes.\par \par \uc2 Today's "emotional move" in the ruble could be considered as an "ideal moment" for locking in profits in long-dollar positions, Mr. Kopeikin from BCS said.\par \par \uc2 "Once the panic stops, we expect the market correlation with oil prices to be restored," said Ms. Orlova from \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Previously, the dollar was gaining one ruble with each $1 decline in oil prices. This means that the ruble's rate of 80 rubles to a dollar corresponds to $30 per barrel, according to Ms. Orlova.\par \par \uc2 "The bad news, however, is that oil still appears to have room to go lower, and we believe that it could touch $20 per barrel. In this case, we would expect the ruble exchange rate to decline to 90-95 per dollar."\par \par \uc2 Still, the Bank of Russia governor \uc2 Elvira Nabiullina\uc2  canceled a planned visit to the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2  in Davos in Switzerland, a person familiar with her schedule said.\par \par \uc2 Russian state-owned media, citing sources close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reported on an emergency meeting Thursday at the bank's headquarters. Market players brooded that it could be similar to the board meeting in December 2014 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would increase the key rate to 17% in the middle of the night.\par \par \uc2 So far, there were few signs of such a meeting. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's headquarters in central Moscow weren't overcrowded with bankers' cars, and the only message the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  published late Thursday was about \uc2 Vneshprombank\uc2 , a lender that was shut down by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 21, 2016 16:03 ET (21:03 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160121ec1l0045c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
