\par\par \b \uc2 Russia Ruble Weakness Breaks Records, Despite Oil Rebound -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dimitra DeFotis   \par \uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2016\par 21:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The Russian ruble reached a level of historical weakness against the U.S. dollar Thursday before recovering somewhat as oil prices moved higher.\par \par \uc2 The Market Vectors Russia exchange-traded fund ( RSX) was up 2% in recent trading as oil prices rallied; Russia's economy depends on oil exports. Still, the ruble remains weak, down 1.2% against the dollar in recent trading. The ruble has tumbled by nearly 12% this month and reached a level of 85 against the dollar Thursday before retreating.\par \par \uc2 The move was stronger than would be implied by oil price moves alone, according to Jonas David, an analyst at UBS Wealth Management. He writes:\par \par \uc2 "Current levels bring us closer to our risk scenario of domestic deposits increasingly being exchanged into dollars. There are few options left to effectively ease the depreciation pressure amid falling oil prices, and policymakers are aware of the high cost of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor \uc2 Elvira Nabiullina\uc2  said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if it sees risks to financial market stability, but at this stage, the bank believes, these are not prevalent. Ultimately, much depends on an eventual stabilization of oil prices ... we therefore see a high likelihood of further bouts of RUB weakness, but reaffirm our view that USDRUB should move below 80.0 again as soon as market conditions moderate and oil prices stabilize. Our USDRUB forecasts are 73.0 in three months and 70.0 in six to 12 months ...\par \par \uc2 Russia's economy remains in recession, and current energy prices imply a sustained contraction ... Policymakers, as indicated by recent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decisions, are prudently assessing growth-inflation dynamics before resuming interest rate cuts ... The next regular policy rate decision is to be announced on 29 January. The current rate of 11% keeps the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  attractive from an interest rate perspective, but weighs on the country's growth prospects. Over the past year, the ruble has taken on an increasingly important role as an external shock absorber for the Russian economy. This makes it more volatile, but also supports the external balance, as shown by the sound current account surplus that Russia runs."\par \par \uc2 Among Russian equities that trade on U.S. exchanges: bank \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  Rossia ( SBRCY) was down fractionally, search giant Yandex ( YNDX) was up 3.4%, payment services company Qiwi ( QIWI) was down 1.6%, oil producer Lukoil ( LUKOY) was up 1.5%, natural gas producer Gazprom ( OGZPY) was down 1% and mining company \uc2 Norilsk Nickel\uc2  ( NILSY) was up 1.7%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Emerging Markets blog, \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/emergingmarketsdaily/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 January 21, 2016 15:52 ET (20:52 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160121ec1l0044p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
