\par\par \b \uc2 Sinking Oil Pushes USD/RUB Above 76 -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 146 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2016\par 10:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0920 GMT At a first glance, the ruble is surprisingly stable on Thursday despite a drop in Brent crude prices towards $32 per barrel. But that's so if checked on the Moscow exchange, which is closed for Orthodox Christmas and will reopen Jan. 11. On the global \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, USD/RUB spiked to 76.07 rubles for the first time since late 2014, according to data from Finam brokerage. More losses in the ruble are likely if oil falls further as \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows no intention of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the sinking \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . USD/RUB is 1.7% higher at 75.54. (andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 07, 2016 04:20 ET (09:20 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160107ec170010g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
