\par\par \b \uc2 Colombians Give Peace Talks Mixed Review -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2015\par 23:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 17:52 EDT - Approval ratings for Colombia's President Juan Manuel Santos jumps from 29% three months ago to 42% now following a recent, major breakthrough in the 3-year-old peace talks with country's largest Marxist guerilla group, according to a Ipsos-Napoleon Franco poll commissioned by Colombian newsmagazine Semana. The latest agreement, on justice for crimes committed during the 50-year civil conflict that has claimed more than 220,000 lives, comes as the majority of Colombians (74%) say they want peace. But they are skeptical that peace can actually be achieved. Some 72% of Colombians say they simply don't trust the rebel group, the \uc2 Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia\uc2 , known as FARC, and 54% say that despite the recent step forward, peace probably won't be signed. Analysts say the results reflect the country's desire for peace, but a so-called "free peace" in which the widely disliked rebels are granted as few concessions as possible. (sara.munoz@wsj.com; @sarasmunoz)\par \par \uc2 2149 GMT - Given poor August and September US employment results, there is no justification for the Fed to hike rates in October, says Elliot Clarke, economist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2 . But with the unemployment rate having fallen near to the level typically viewed as consistent with full employment, a moderation in the pace of jobs growth is not necessarily a major concern for policy makers if jobs growth stabilizes at a still-robust rate, which it is, he adds. December remains a likely choice for a first hike, Clarke says, adding that: "To do otherwise, without a further marked deterioration, would cast doubt over the FOMC's policy mechanism and the likely outlook for US growth, with material flow-on consequences for markets." (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 2144 GMT - \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  succinctly sums up the challenge facing \uc2 Gryphon Minerals\uc2  (GRY.AU), which aims to build the Banfora gold mine in Burkina Faso. "Banfora's risk/return trade off appears unacceptable at current gold price levels," analyst Michael Slifirski says. The broker slashes its price target by 74% to 7 Australian cents, and says its outperform call lacks conviction. The spot gold price is now well below the project's planning price of US$1,250/oz, and \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  worries that further meaningful cost cuts may be hard to achieve. "Management appears to have taken the project as far as they can with progression to development now reliant on securing a funding package, which itself appears dependent on a gold price recovery," Slifirski says. GRY last at 5 Australian cents. (david.winning@wsj.com; @dwinningWSJ)\par \par \uc2 17:42 EDT - \uc2 Media General\uc2  (MEG) hires new bankers and lawyers to weigh a $1.9B takeover bid from Nexstar (NXST), which aims to bust up MEG's $2.4B agreement to buy Meredith (MDP). That's likely because MEG's current advisers could be seen as biased toward the original deal -- particularly investment bank RBC, which has committed to finance the MDP transaction. Lending fees typically dwarf those from sell-side advisory engagements, so bringing on \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  and Weil Gotshal wipes away any hint of a conflict. Boards are under increasing pressure to ensure their advisers are above reproach, following a rash of shareholder lawsuits alleging conflicts of interest that shortchanged investors. (liz.hoffman@wsj.com; @lizrhoffman)\par \par \uc2 17:40 EDT - What will knock crude oil out of the $44-$47/bbl range it's been stuck in since Sept. 1? Gabriel Collins, an attorney at \uc2 Baker and Hostetler\uc2  in Houston, says it could be \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Syria, and says prices could tumble toward $30/bbl by the new year. "Amid worries that \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's armed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Syria signals a new Cold War between \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the West, another and related rematch appears in the offing," he says on OilPro. "If Russia and Iran are Syrian President Assad's strongest foreign backers, Saudi Arabia and its Gulf Arab allies surely number among his and Iran's most implacable foes. The implications of a potential Russo-Saudi proxy war for international oil markets are significant." (dan.molinski@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 2138 GMT - The Australian dollar may work its way back towards near-term resistance should the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue to endorse a wait-and-see approach for monetary policy at its policy meeting, says David Song, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at DailyFX. A survey of 11 economist by WSJ shows all expect no change in the cash rate target, now at 2%. Despite below-trend growth in the economy, the RBA may continue to endorse a wait-and-see approach as the depreciation in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to support growth, particularly through a larger contribution from net service exports, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may stick to the sidelines throughout 2015, he adds. Policy decision due at 0330 GMT. (james.glynn@wsj.com; @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 17:36 EDT - \uc2 Caterpillar\uc2  (CAT) is among the US exporters most bullish about the new Trans-Pacific Partnership deal. If the deal is ratified, CAT says, Vietnam's 15% import tariff on bulldozers would be eliminated, for example, saving buyers of \uc2 Caterpillar\uc2 's D-8 models $150,000. In Malaysia, tariffs of 30% on engines and 15% on spare parts would vanish. CAT says the trade deal generally would spur trade. CAT closed up 5.3% to $69.17. (bob.hagerty@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 17:23 EDT - It's one of the most persistent debates in the oil market: Is gasoline consumption driven by oil prices, or by economic growth? Clearview Energy Partners crunches some numbers and tentatively comes down on the side of price. "In the ten states responsible for roughly 60% of year-on-year US gasoline consumption growth, consumption gains appear more closely linked to price decreases than to structural factors such as declining unemployment rates and rising personal incomes," the firm says. "As such, a rebound in global crude prices may have potential to reverse these consumption gains." (nicole.friedman@wsj.com; @NicoleFriedman)\par \par \uc2 17:22 EDT - Investors are underestimating the potential boost to Donaco's (DNA.AU) earnings from the casino operator's deal with China's Heng Sheng Group at the Star Vegas casino in Cambodia, says Canaccord Genuity. The deal, which likely means more Chinese nationals traveling to Donaco's casino, boosts the number of gambling tables at the venue by 28% to 137. "While our current estimates for annualized ebitda of A$10 million reflect 'base case' assumptions, our 'bull case' indicates the Heng Sheng VIP room could be more than 20% EPS accretive in FY17," analyst Aaron Muller says. The broker keeps a buy call on Donaco and A$1.54/share price target. DNA last at A$0.69. (david.winning@wsj.com; @dwinningWSJ)\par \par \uc2 17:20 EDT - \uc2 BP\uc2  agrees to pay a record $20B to resolve all federal and state claims against the company over its role in the Deepwater Horizon oil spill. Under the terms of the finalized deal announced by the Justice Department today, \uc2 BP\uc2  won't have to pay all the money at once. Softening the hit to its cash flow, the company is able to spread out payments over a 15-year period. The last installments are due in 2031, more than 21 years after the Deepwater Horizon disaster, which killed 11 crew members and caused the largest oil spill in US waters. The two biggest pieces of the settlement are the $5.5B in Clean Water Act penalties and the $7.1B that \uc2 BP\uc2  agreed to pay to the US and Gulf Coast states to cover long-term environmental damages. The total settlement figure also includes $1B that \uc2 BP\uc2  previously committed for early restoration projects. (jacob.gershman@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 17:19 EDT - Ruling in favor of a former \uc2 UBS\uc2  employee, Connecticut's highest court says today that public and private employees in the state are shielded by speech rights more expansive than the First Amendment. The Connecticut Supreme Court rules that government and private-sector employers are barred from punishing workers for statements they make as part of their jobs on matters of important public concern. At issue was a complaint brought against \uc2 UBS\uc2  by a former employee who questioned the valuation of properties held in \uc2 UBS\uc2 's real-estate investment arm. A UBS spokeswoman said the company "believes that Mr. Trusz's claims are wholly without merit, and the firm did not improperly act against him." She said \uc2 UBS\uc2  would continue to "vigorously" defend itself in the matter. Wesley W. Horton, a lawyer for Trusz, says today's decision is the first by a state high court that gives "employees a free-speech right to speak out in an area that involves their official duties." (jacob.gershman@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 2114 GMT - Weak inflation will likely drive \uc2 New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut its policy rate by another 25 bps to 2.5% by year-end, says Christina Leung, senior economist at the New Zealand Institute of Economic Research. She says a rate cut in October, however, "is a line-ball" call, and the RBNZ might opt to hold off until December. She says an official cash rate at 2.5% is an "emergency setting" and she doesn't expect rates to go any lower. (rebecca.howard@wsj.com; @FarroHoward)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 October 05, 2015 17:52 ET (21:52 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020151005eba5003i7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
