\par\par \b \uc2 Kremlin Aide Says Bank of Russia Should Limit Ruble's Rebound\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2015\par 11:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Bank of Russia should consider resuming purchases of dollars and euros for the country's reserves once the ruble strengthens beyond 60 to the dollar, presidential aide Andrey Belousov said Friday.\par \par \uc2 "There will be a need to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the ruble strengthens too much...I think if the dollar falls below 60 [rubles], than it's time to start," Interfax news agency quoted Mr. Belousov as saying.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia let the ruble float in 2014 after spending billions of dollars in fruitless attempts to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling rapidly under pressure from Western sanctions and falling oil prices.\par \par \uc2 The banks has repeatedly said it targets no specific ruble level but other officials have repeatedly indicated that Russia isn't interested in a strong ruble as the weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  helps to offset the negative impact of low oil prices on the budget.\par \par \uc2 After buying up to $200 million a day from mid-May, which helped to ease pressure on the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to halt daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late July as the ruble got a hit from falling oil prices. The ruble has lost around 45% of its value compared with a year ago.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had previously said it was planning to bring the level of gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves back to "comfortable" levels of $500 billion in the next three to five years by purchasing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the local market.\par \par \uc2 The ruble was 0.7% weaker at 67.65 versus the dollar as of 0845 GMT on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 04-09-15 0932GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020150904eb940006d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
