\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russian rouble gains against dollar on higher oil prices\b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2015\par 10:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background, analyst)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Aug 4 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble strengthened on Tuesday, supported by an upturn in oil prices, after hitting new five-month lows in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices have fallen more than 3 percent this week on oversupply worries, pushing the rouble to its weakest against the dollar since March 11.\par \par \uc2 At 0700 GMT, the rouble was 0.5 percent stronger against the dollar at around 63.21 and had gained 0.4 percent to 69.30 versus the euro.\par \par \uc2 International oil benchmark Brent was up 1.1 percent to $50.07 per barrel, despite output from the \uc2 Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries\uc2  reaching its highest monthly level in recent history in July.\par \par \uc2 A further fall in oil prices could deepen Russia's economic downturn, with growth already hit by lower prices for the country's main export and Western sanctions over Moscow's role in the Ukraine crisis.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  said on Monday sanctions could cost Russian 9 percent of its gross domestic product. The Fund forecast "weak" economic growth of about 1.5 percent annually in the medium term, compared to Russia's 7 percent yearly growth before the 2008 global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 ING economist Dmitry Polevoy said a further slide in oil prices could push the rouble to 68-70 against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The real intrigue is how the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will act," he said in a note to traders. "Will they see the weakened rouble as a threat to financial stability? If so, everything is possible, from an increase in the limit of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  repurchasing to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week stopped \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to replenish its international reserves because of a rise in market volatility. The regulator said on Monday there was no set rouble rate at which it would restart buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lower oil price also weighed on Russian stock indexes. The dollar-based RTS, which is closely linked to the rouble, was down 0.21 percent to 833 points while the rouble-based MICEX .MCX edged up 0.05 percent to 1,664 points.\par \par \uc2 For rouble poll data see reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 -polls?RIC=RUB=\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 Russia in graphics: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/dun63s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/dun63s}}}\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Jack Stubbs; Editing by Katya Golubkova and Janet Lawrence) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-8-4T09:10:09.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150804eb8400a6s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
