\par\par \b \uc2 Romania - Factors to watch on June 15\b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2015\par 08:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, June 15 (Reuters) - Here are news stories, press reports and events to watch which may affect Romanian financial markets on Monday.                              \par \par \uc2 DEBT TENDER               \par \par \uc2 Romanian debt managers tender 300 million lei ($75.06 million) worth of June 2019 treasury bonds.                              \par \par \uc2 CURRENT ACCOUNT               \par \par \uc2 Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release January-April current account balance data.                              \par \par \uc2 NO CONFIDENCE VOTE               \par \par \uc2 Victor Ponta's leftist government easily survived a no-confidence motion in Romania's parliament as expected on Friday, securing the prime minister's political immunity in a criminal investigation.                              \par \par \uc2 CEE MARKETS               \par \par \uc2 Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government bonds eased slightly on Friday after Greece's talks with creditors hit a stalemate in the latest twist of its debt crisis.               \par \par \uc2 Romania's leu eased 0.2 percent to 4.472 against the euro, failing to benefit from the victory of Romania's leftist government in a no-confidence vote in parliament.               \par \par \uc2 RAIFFEISEN               \par \par \uc2 Raiffeisen Bank International\uc2 's business in Russia is doing well despite the weak local economy and political tensions over Ukraine, the Austrian bank's chairman told Kurier newspaper.               \par \par \uc2 Walter Rothensteiner\uc2  said it aimed to grow in Romania, the Czech Republic and Slovakia.                              \par \par \uc2 US HEAVY ARMS               \par \par \uc2 The United States plans to store heavy military equipment in the Baltics and Eastern European nations to reassure allies unnerved by \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine and to deter further aggression, U.S. officials said.                              \par \par \uc2 WHEAT TENDER               \par \par \uc2 Egypt's state grain buyer, the \uc2 General Authority for Supply Commodities\uc2  (GASC), said on Friday it had bought 180,000 tonnes of Russian and Romanian wheat in a tender for July 11-20 shipment.               \par \par \uc2 For a schedule of forthcoming Romanian events, double click , and a calendar of east European economic indicators, see.               \par \par \uc2 \f2  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par  Romanian equities     RO-E     E.Europe equities     .CEE\par  Romanian money        RO-M     Romaniandebt          RO-D\par  Eastern Europe        EEU      All emerging markets  EMRG\par  Hot stocks            HOT      Stock markets         STX\par  Market debt news      DBT      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news            FRX\par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par ($1 = 3.9968 lei) \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-6-15T07:33:39.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150615eb6f007ad\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
