\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  Steps Up  \highlight22\uc2 Interventions \highlight\uc2  as Ruble Firms\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2015\par 09:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased its purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the country's reserves as the ruble continued recovering on Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which reports its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a lag of two working days, bought $200 million on Tuesday after buying $150 million the previous day. Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an attempt to beef up depleted reserves on May 13, it has purchased up to $3.58 billion.\par \par \uc2 Last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it wanted to bring gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves back to $500 billion, an amount last seen in early 2014 before Russia annexed Crimea and oil prices plummeted from around $100 a barrel. As of May 29, Russia's reserves stood at $356.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 To hedge the crisis-struck economy against capital flight and new shocks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to boost reserves in the next three to five years, suggesting that pressure limiting the ruble recovery would be in place for a long while.\par \par \uc2 In early trading Thursday, the ruble shed 0.3% to 54.48 against the dollar but was still some way from the 57.2 it hit late last week, its weakest level in 