\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Russia Deputy Head Expects Rates To Be Cut Further--Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh   \par \uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 2015\par 16:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW--Russia is committed to making further interest rate cuts and building its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 "We hope that the circumstances will allow us to do it [cut rates] further," First Deputy Chairman \uc2 Dmitry Tulin\uc2  said, Interfax news agency reported on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Facing a record selloff in the ruble late last year, the Bank of Russia had to increase the key rate to 17%. In an attempt to limit economic contraction, ignited by a drop in oil prices and Western sanctions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has cut rates three times this year, bringing the key rate to 12.5%.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tulin also said that the country's international reserves are close to comfortable levels, at least "at the edge" of the comfort zone.\par \par \uc2 And the bank's First Deputy Chairwoman Ksenia Yudayeva said Tuesday she would like reserves to grow higher, Interfax reported.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia started purchasing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market on May 13, aiming to replenish the country's reserves. Over the past year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent billions of dollars to defend the plummeting ruble.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would buy between $100 million and $200 million a day, but could raise the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the future. \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international reserves rose $3.8 billion to $362.3 billion in the week to May 15. A year ago reserves stood at $466.8 billion.\par \par \uc2 The market is closely looking for any indication that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will start buying more foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The bank's next rate decision is due on June 15.\par \par \uc2 Write to Andrey Ostroukh at andrey.ostroukh@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 26, 2015 10:10 ET (14:10 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150526eb5q00213\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
